#: ../../tools/drug_synergy_tools.rst 67c0d9d5747d47569d3841e9af264b4c
msgid "DrugSynergy_calculate_loewe tool specification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/drug_synergy_tools.rst:178 f8ab7ccc99b74d2dae1765c8ba44824f
msgid "**Name**: ``DrugSynergy_calculate_loewe``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/drug_synergy_tools.rst:180 268b2fe5ab2e4057906c89f2c981daff
msgid ""
"**Description**: Calculate Loewe Additivity synergy score for a drug "
"combination. The Loewe model is the most widely used reference model for "
"drug interaction: d\\_a/D\\_a(E) + d\\_b/D\\_b(E) = 1 at additivity. If "
"sum < 1, the combination is synergistic (needs less drug than expected); "
"if > 1, it is antagonistic. Requires single-agent dose-response data for "
"each drug (to fit Hill curves) plus the combination doses and observed "
"effect. Based on Loewe & Muischnek (1926). Use for: rigorous synergy "
"quantification with dose-response data, comparison with Bliss/HSA/ZIP "
"models."
msgstr ""

